cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the specific VERSION you used —
  each release is archived with its own DOI, and results can differ
  between versions. The model it implements is described in Simha et al.
  (2026); please cite that paper for the science (see references below).
title: "Muscle Spindle Model — Interactive Tutorial"
abstract: >-
  An interactive, tutorial-style MATLAB app for the biophysical muscle
  spindle model of Simha et al. (2026). It exposes the model's inputs,
  intermediate signals, and Ia receptor potential for exploration, and
  fits fusimotor (gamma) drive to recorded afferent activity.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Simha
    given-names: Surabhi N.
    affiliation: "Neuromechanics Lab, Emory University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SurabhiSimha/spindleModelTutorial"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-30"
keywords:
  - muscle spindle
  - proprioception
  - Ia afferent
  - cross-bridge model
  - fusimotor drive
  - MATLAB

# No preferred-citation: GitHub's "Cite this repository" button shows the
# preferred citation when one exists, which would surface the paper instead of
# the software. The paper is listed under references so it stays in the
# metadata without displacing the software citation.
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      The mammalian muscle spindle as a tunable feedback controller in
      locomotion
    authors:
      - family-names: Simha
        given-names: Surabhi
      - family-names: Sawicki
        given-names: Gregory
      - family-names: Cope
        given-names: Timothy
      - family-names: Ting
        given-names: Lena
    journal: bioRxiv
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.64898/2026.07.03.736206
